hips out of position. Raising would isolate the opponent but bloats the pot with a hand that plays better with high implied odds in a smaller pot.\n\nReason: With 98 off-suit in the Big Blind facing a limp, the most standard and mathematically sound play is to check. This allows you to see a flop for free and re-evaluate based on the community cards. There is no need to inflate the pot pre-flop with a marginal hand.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
